        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Timothy Day",
          "email": "timday@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-06-16 20:27:04.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20385 osd-zfs: use object id directly instead of zc_zapobj",
        "message": "LU-20385 osd-zfs: use object id directly instead of zc_zapobj\n\nReplace references to it->ozi_zc->zc_zapobj with the directory object\nid in osd_dir_it_rec() (via it->ozi_obj->oo_dn->dn_object) and in\nosd_scan_dir() (via the id parameter).\n\nSourcing the id from the object rather than the cursor is a no-op\nchange. A ZAP is a single DMU object and the cursor's zc_zapobj\nis always set to the same directory object the cursor was opened\non (dn_object / the id parameter).\n\nZFS commit efda1093ffa8 (\"zap: add zap_cursor_init_by_dnode() & rework cursor resource lifetime\")\ndeprecates this field. Lustre is the only remaining caller.\n\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I0bfa061a0f2225374338fdda02a56bcc1f805484\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
